            <div xml:id="d744">

                <pb facs="1034" n="914" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg914"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2684: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chargé in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Whitehouse</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-09-07T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 7,
                                1922—4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>278. Your No. 350, September 5, 1 p.m.</p>
                <p>Phrase “The Powers other than China” is intended to refer to the five Powers
                    party to the agreement of January, 1919. The additional Powers who participated
                    in the Washington resolutions have no direct substantial interest in the matter
                    and it appears inadvisable in the opinion of this Government to extend the basis
                    of the 1919 agreement. The participation of the additional Powers in the
                    discussions at Washington arose entirely fortuitously as a result of their
                    presence in the Conference for other purposes.</p>
                <p>Present proposals do not contemplate a new international agreement as seems to be
                    indicated in your telegram but look merely to the presentation at Peking by the
                    five Powers of identic notes in the sense of the memorandum already
                    submitted.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
